  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kyrgyzstan: Assistance to the Government of the Kyrgyz Republic in Joining the United Nations Convention on International Settlement Agreements Resulting from Mediation (the &#x2018;Singapore Convention on Mediation&#x2019;)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1) To conduct legislative and institutional analysis of the readiness to implement the Singapore Convention and advise on lessons learned from the experience of other states that joined the Convention. 2) To provide assistance in preparation of necessary legislative and regulatory changes to join the Singapore Convention as defined by the Kyrgyz Law as well as within the process of signing the Convention. 3) To further capacity development of the key players for implementation of the Convention such as judges, mediators, professional lawyers, enforcement officers and business. 4) To implement a targeted awareness-raising campaign and consensus-building concerning the adoption of the Convention.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Direct beneficiaries: Ministry of Justice, judges, lawyers, mediators and enforcement officers. Indirect beneficiaries: Businesses and investors</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to assist the Government of the Kyrgyz Republic in the process of joining and implementing the Singapore Convention on Mediation.</narrative>
  </description>
